      ],
      "requirement": "Keep Huxley’s classification memorandum and Darwin’s 3 October reply in their actual directions. Huxley’s surviving text defines classification and rejects equating Darwin’s pedigree work with pure zoology; Darwin then says he did not expect an answer and poses a new theoretical case. Preserve the missing earlier question and do not reverse the edge because the topics overlap.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "id": "DCP-LETT-2144",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "Cuviers definition of the object of Classification seems to me to embody all that is really wanted in Science",
          "dom_locator": "#letter .body-content > p:nth-of-type(1)"
        },
        {
          "id": "DCP-LETT-2150",
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "quote": "I know you have no time for speculative correspondence; & I did not in the least expect an answer to my last.",
          "dom_locator": "#letter .body-content > p:nth-of-type(4)"
        }
      ],
      "date_voice_hold": "2144 is Huxley incoming with a broad before-3 October bound; 2150 is Darwin outgoing on 3 October. Preserve direction and response scope.",
